{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-023-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ExplosionFxTests.cs","line":455,"method":"ShouldTriggerExplosion_PassesButWarpSuppresses_LogsSuppression","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.WarpLoopPolicy.cs:101; flip the comparison to < -> red","what_it_asserts":"ShouldTriggerExplosion returns true for a Destroyed ghost, and ShouldSuppressVisualFx returns true at 50/100/1000x.","why_weak":"The name promises a suppression log assertion; neither helper logs and no log line is asserted. The suppression half duplicates ShouldSuppressVisualFx_Above10x_Suppresses with extra rates.","proposed_action":"Rename to ShouldSuppressVisualFx_AboveThreshold_Suppresses and fold the rates into the existing theory, or assert the actual call-site coupling (GhostPlaybackEngine.cs:1092) instead.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
