{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-023-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/EngineIterTraceTests.cs","line":293,"method":"EmitEngineIterTrace_Renders_Combined_Input_And_Outcome_Tokens","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"medium","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackEngine.cs:675; drop the prefix from FormatEngineIterMessage -> both red","what_it_asserts":"A hand-concatenated entry+outcome string passed to EmitEngineIterTrace appears in the rendered log line with the engine-frame-iter token.","why_weak":"Production never performs this concatenation in the exercised path (it lives in EmitEngineIterTraceForFrame, not called here); the emit contract is already pinned by the twin at line 339.","proposed_action":"Either drop it or move the assertion onto EmitEngineIterTraceForFrame so the per-index entry+outcome pairing is actually production-produced.","effort":"M","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-023-04","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ExplosionFxTests.cs","line":322,"method":"ApplyDestroyedFallback_WasDestroyed_AlreadyDestroyed_NoChange","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/ParsekFlight.TerminalEvents.cs:328; delete the already-Destroyed early return -> red","what_it_asserts":"ApplyDestroyedFallback returns false and leaves TerminalStateValue at Destroyed when it is already Destroyed.","why_weak":"Production sets rec.VesselDestroyed=true unconditionally at :326 before that return; no test in the file asserts it, so deleting that line leaves all five ApplyDestroyedFallback tests green even though SwitchSegmentNoOpClassifier reads the bool.","proposed_action":"Add Assert.True(rec.VesselDestroyed) to the wasDestroyed cases and Assert.False on the not-destroyed cases.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"ParsekFlight.ApplyDestroyedFallback","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/ParsekFlight.TerminalEvents.cs","sut_line":326,"case_kind":"state-transition","proposed_name":"ApplyDestroyedFallback_WasDestroyed_SetsVesselDestroyedFlag","sketch":"Recording with TerminalStateValue already Destroyed and VesselDestroyed=false; call ApplyDestroyedFallback(true, rec); assert rec.VesselDestroyed is true even though the method returns false.","guards":"A destruction with no onPartDie Destroyed PartEvent would leave VesselDestroyed false and let SwitchSegmentNoOpClassifier auto-discard the destroyed resume as a no-op.","risk":"recording"}
